    "content": "The Federal Government of Somalia has issued a strong condemnation of a terrorist attack targeting a church in Jordan, according to a statement released on Monday. The attack, which occurred on [date], has drawn widespread international outrage. Somalia's government expressed its solidarity with the people and government of Jordan and extended condolences to the families of the victims.\n\nThe statement did not specify the details of the attack or the group responsible, but it reiterated Somalia's stance against all forms of terrorism. Somalia has faced its own struggles with terrorism, particularly from the militant group Al-Shabaab, which has carried out numerous attacks in the country. The government's condemnation reflects its commitment to combating extremism both domestically and internationally.\n\nJordan has been a target of terrorist attacks in the past, including a 2016 attack in Karak that killed 14 people. The recent attack on a church underscores the persistent threat posed by extremist groups in the region. Somali officials have often emphasized the need for global unity in the fight against terrorism, and this condemnation aligns with that position.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this attack resonates deeply. Many Somalis living abroad, including in Jordan, maintain strong ties to their homeland and are affected by global security developments. The diaspora has been a crucial source of remittances and support for Somalia, and incidents like this highlight the shared challenges faced by communities worldwide. Somali communities in Jordan and elsewhere have expressed solidarity with the victims and condemned the violence.\n\nThe Somali government's condemnation also serves as a reminder of the importance of international cooperation in countering terrorism. Somalia has been working with international partners to strengthen its security forces and address the root causes of extremism. The attack in Jordan is a stark reminder that terrorism knows no borders and requires a collective response.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/soomaaliya-oo-cambaaraysay-weerar-lagu-qaaday-kaniisad-ku-taalla-dalka-urdun/426789/",
